findings.description:
Every changed line spells out `dark-light-choose(scale-color($primary, $lightness: N%), scale-color($secondary, $lightness: (100-N)%))` by hand. The complement is derivable, yet it is typed manually each time. That is the mechanism behind the four inconsistencies above, and review cannot easily tell intentional deviations from typos.

A small helper next to `dark-light-choose` and `dark-light-diff` would remove the duplication, for example:

```scss
@function primary-scaled($lightness) {
  @return dark-light-choose(
    scale-color($primary, $lightness: $lightness),
    scale-color($secondary, $lightness: 100% - $lightness)
  );
}
```

The handful of non-mirrored pairs could stay explicit, which would make them visibly deliberate.
